WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.983
Cat meowed and hissed.

2
00:00:04.984 --> 00:00:09.302
She jumped at the swans.

3
00:00:09.303 --> 00:00:11.999
"What's she doing?" Tom said.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.478
"Those swans are mean!"

5
00:00:14.479 --> 00:00:17.327
The swans flew at Cat.

6
00:00:17.328 --> 00:00:19.376
They tried to bite her.

7
00:00:19.377 --> 00:00:23.311
Cat ran back toward the other carriages.

8
00:00:23.312 --> 00:00:29.094
The swans chased her.

9
00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:33.173
Walter waved his wand again and again.

10
00:00:33.174 --> 00:00:37.620
His king shouted loudly.

11
00:00:37.621 --> 00:00:40.838
The swans chased Cat.

12
00:00:40.839 --> 00:00:45.829
She jumped in front of the next carriage.

13
00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:51.275
Crash! Boom! All the carriages crashed into Walter's carriage.

14
00:00:51.276 --> 00:00:54.430
It was a royal mess.

15
00:00:54.431 --> 00:01:00.090
The kings yelled at each other.

16
00:01:00.091 --> 00:01:05.273
The wizards cast spells.

17
00:01:05.274 --> 00:01:09.457
Tom looked at his king. "Let's go, Your Majesty!"

18
00:01:09.458 --> 00:01:13.296
The king picked up the reins.

19
00:01:13.297 --> 00:01:20.307
He drove carefully around all the other carriages.

20
00:01:20.308 --> 00:01:25.724
Soon his carriage crossed the finish line.

21
00:01:25.725 --> 00:01:35.578
"I won!" the king shouted.

22
00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:39.586
"No fair!" grumbled the other kings.

23
00:01:39.587 --> 00:01:41.697
"My carriage is faster!"

24
00:01:41.698 --> 00:01:47.161
"No, mine is faster!"

25
00:01:47.162 --> 00:01:50.683
Cat jumped into Tom's pocket.

26
00:01:50.684 --> 00:01:53.692
"Are you hurt?" Tom asked.

27
00:01:53.693 --> 00:01:57.185
"Those swans are very mean!"

28
00:01:57.186 --> 00:01:59.226
Cat licked a paw.

29
00:01:59.227 --> 00:02:02.859
"The swans are very mean," she said.

30
00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.085
"But they are not very smart.

31
00:02:05.086 --> 00:02:11.691
It was easy to get away."

32
00:02:11.692 --> 00:02:14.312
"Good job, Tom," said May.

33
00:02:14.313 --> 00:02:18.974
Walter glared at Tom. "You were lucky this year.

34
00:02:18.975 --> 00:02:22.075
Next year my king will win!"

35
00:02:22.076 --> 00:02:30.764
Tom smiled. "We'll see about that!"

